From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_LATE_DEREFS=1 lowers indirect derefs after optimizing

Driver patch, after lead-mesh-10. Off unless the switch is set. From exploitizm/PS5_Mesa 8b4cdfb897, which
does this without a switch.

The compute pass lowers indirect derefs before its first optimization loop, which RADV's graphics stages never
do. exploitizm reports a builder out of memory in nir_opt_copy_prop_vars on Ocarina's mesh shaders without a
task shader, in two runs, one with the heap at 0.9 GiB in use and the pool not short, and that this order
stopped it. Ours has the same line, and the T47 env runs that path (EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_LONE=1). Whether
it played a part in T47's or T48's cold deaths is not known.

RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_LONE_REVISION stays as it is on purpose, and the switch isn't in the hash. Both orders do the
same work, so cached copies stay good, and raising it would cost another cold boot. The switch only acts on
pipelines that actually compile. radv-build-id is pinned to the Mesa revision, so this patch doesn't change the
driver's cache UUID either.

Compiled with the driver's flags, syntax only. Not linked, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_mesh_compute.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_mesh_compute.c
index 119abaa..b52cea7 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_mesh_compute.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_mesh_compute.c
@@ -581,9 +581,23 @@ radv_mesh_compute_compile(const struct radv_compiler_info *compiler_info, struct
    nir->info.max_subgroup_size = 32;
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_compute_system_values, &compute_sysval_options);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_global_vars_to_local);
-   NIR_PASS(_, nir, ac_nir_lower_indirect_derefs);
+   /* EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_LATE_DEREFS=1: indirect derefs after the optimization loop, as the
+    * graphics stages have them (radv_graphics_shaders_compile). Lowered first, a mesh shader's arrays
+    * indexed by vertex or primitive become if-ladders before they can be optimized, and copy
+    * propagation of variables can run out of memory on the result. */
+   const char *const late_asked = getenv("EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_LATE_DEREFS");
+   const bool late_derefs = late_asked && late_asked[0] == '1';
+   if (!late_derefs)
+      NIR_PASS(_, nir, ac_nir_lower_indirect_derefs);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_vars_to_ssa);
    radv_optimize_nir(nir, stage.key.optimisations_disabled);
+   if (late_derefs) {
+      bool derefs_lowered = false;
+      NIR_PASS(derefs_lowered, nir, ac_nir_lower_indirect_derefs);
+      NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_vars_to_ssa);
+      if (derefs_lowered && !stage.key.optimisations_disabled)
+         radv_optimize_nir(nir, false);
+   }
    nir_shader_gather_info(nir, nir_shader_get_entrypoint(nir));
 
    radv_nir_shader_info_init(MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE, MESA_SHADER_NONE, &stage.info);
